  "scenario": {
    "pdf_page": 6,
    "figure_or_table": "Table 3 (Case 3 benchmark configuration), with Table 6 (thermal-aware results, page 7) and Fig. 5 (Case 3 layouts, page 8)",
    "description": "ATPlace2.5D benchmark Case 3: 8 dies, x32 bump type, 8448 nets, 39 mm x 39 mm interposer, whitespace 0.6 as printed in Table 3. Fig. 5 caption gives CPU 9 x 8 mm^2 and DRAM 9 x 9 mm^2. The pinned PKU-IDEA/ATPlace_pub Case3 files give 4 CPU2 blocks (8000 x 9000 um) and 4 DRAM blocks (9000 x 9000 um) with 150 W per CPU and 20 W per DRAM. The pinned Case3.pl holds only placeholder (0,0) coordinates, so no final placement is published in the packet.",
    "architecture": "2.5D-IC with a passive interposer on an organic substrate; 4 CPU chiplets and 4 DRAM chiplets with UCIe x32 advanced-package D2D links; primary heat path through TIM, heat spreader and air-forced heatsink; HotSpot 6.0 as the golden thermal simulator.",
    "workload": "Worst-case static power distribution per chiplet (pinned Case3.power: CPU2_0..3 = 150 W each, DRAM_0..3 = 20 W each); no power time series.",
    "operating_point": "Steady-state, ambient 45 C, heatsink convective resistance 0.1 K/W per the paper (page 3; the pinned hotspot.config has r_convec 0.01 K/W, a discrepancy). Reported Case 3 thermal-aware Tmax is 92.3 C for ATPlace2.5D and 94.1 C for TAP-2.5D (Table 6, page 7).",
    "steady_2d_relevant": true
  },
  "original_setup": {
    "solver": "HotSpot 6.0 steady-state grid model (64x64 grid) is the golden thermal simulator (PDF p.3). During optimization, ATPlace2.5D uses a physics-based analytical compact thermal model (Green's-function type, 2N+3 fitted parameters) trained on HotSpot maps of 5-10 legalized layouts (PDF pp.4-5). Heat leaves through the TIM, spreader and air-forced heatsink path, with adiabatic lateral walls, 45 C ambient and 0.1 K/W convective resistance (PDF p.3).",
    "optimizer": "Analytical orientation-aware placement. A MILP (Gurobi) gives the initial placement. Conjugate gradient descent (Polak-Ribiere) then minimizes wirelength + lambda_therm*R[T] + lambda_dens*density penalty, with noise perturbation when stuck. A MILP legalization follows, and Optuna Bayesian optimization tunes hyperparameters (PDF pp.4-6).",
    "controller": "None. This is static design-time chiplet placement under worst-case steady-state power, with no runtime or dynamic thermal controller or power-time-series control.",
    "benchmark": "ATPlace2.5D constructed benchmark Case 3 (Table 3, PDF p.6): 8 dies (4 CPU, 4 DRAM), x32 UCIe bump type, 8448 nets, 39 mm x 39 mm interposer, whitespace listed as 0.6. Thermal-aware results are in Table 6 (PDF p.7) and layouts in Fig. 5 (PDF p.8). Pinned PKU-IDEA/ATPlace_pub Case3 files (commit 782b89b) give block dimensions and powers: CPU2_0..3 are 8000x9000 um at 150 W each, and DRAM_0..3 are 9000x9000 um at 20 W each. Case3.pl contains only placeholder (0,0) coordinates, so no final placement is published."
  },
