  "physical_mismatches": [
    {
      "reason": "The original package is a heterogeneous 3D stack: passive interposer with TSVs, RDL, microbump layer, epoxy fill, C4 pillars and organic substrate. A simple 2D steady-state chiplet model cannot reproduce this vertical structure or its layer-wise conductivities, and the layer properties are inherited from refs [6,36] rather than listed in the packet.",
      "essential": true
    },
    {
      "reason": "The paper's cooling is an air-forced heatsink with 0.1 K/W convective resistance, spreader and sink edges 2x the interposer, and 45 C ambient (PDF p.3). The pinned hotspot.config instead has r_convec 0.01 K/W, s_spreader 0.03 m, s_sink 0.06 m, ambient 318.15 K, block model type and secondary path off, so the cooling boundary conditions differ and the paper's Tmax cannot be matched numerically.",
      "essential": true
    },
    {
      "reason": "The original solver is HotSpot 6.0 on a 64x64 grid, plus a fitted analytical compact model that is least accurate at chiplet edges and the interposer boundary (MAE about 1.2 C overall). A different thermal solver will not reproduce the paper's Tmax.",
      "essential": true
    },
    {
